Implement the assigned slice from docs/superhuman-browsing-implementation-plan.md in this thread's isolated worktree. Read that plan, the source browsing UX spec, ADR 0001, development guide, existing slice contracts, and repository instructions first. The source branch is feat/ux-05-safe-bulk-processing at 6c30b9c; UX-06/07 and other later slices may not exist here. Inspect actual prerequisites rather than assuming another thread's changes are available. Do not merge/cherry-pick other active threads or reimplement unrelated roadmap slices wholesale; if a dependency prevents safe implementation, record the concrete blocker and ask for the needed decision. Implement the useful independently testable portion with explicit capability boundaries, not dead controls.

Create a narrow slice implementation contract and acceptance checklist, then implement and test the vertical journey across Vue, typed IPC, Rust/SQLite, synthetic provider/browser fixtures as applicable. Preserve stable account+ID targets, durable intent/recovery, bulk/Undo correctness, no-auto-read, safe plain text, permissions, retained snapshots, local-only drafts and normal-close protections. Keep Rust-generated TypeScript generated; update command registrations/permissions and transport tests for IPC changes. Use existing project check/build tasks per development guide. Record headless/browser evidence separately from native Mac/provider validation; do not claim native or remote convergence from fakes. Read applicable frontend skill before UI work. Do the work yourself; do not launch subagents or additional threads.

